
# JVM heap dumps. A 754 MB one was committed in the first AuntieOS commit and
# had to be purged from history to push at all. They are build debris, they can
# contain whatever was in memory at the time (tokens, PII), and they are far
# over GitHub's 100 MB limit.
*.hprof
.release-state
# The function names the last release actually shipped. Per machine, like
# .release-state, and read for the same reason: to tell what production holds
# that this code no longer does.
.release-functions
# Per-run release logs and the running-release pidfile, written by
# scripts/release-bg.sh. Machine-local by nature: they record what one operator's
# machine did on one night, and the durable record of a release is its tag.
.release-logs/
__pycache__/
node_modules/
node_modules
# ui-ideas holds design authority source 2 (auntieos-admin/CLAUDE.md). It was
# ignored wholesale, so a clone and every git worktree contained none of it,
# while the plans cite it as the spec. The HTML is now tracked, scrubbed of the
# real client names that were the original reason for the exclusion.
# The IMAGES stay out: they cannot be scrubbed by find-and-replace, one of them
# is a third-party product screenshot carrying someone's booking data, and they
# are 26 MB against 1.8 MB of text.
# Leading `**/` is required. A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the
# directory holding this .gitignore, so a bare `ui-ideas/**/*.png` would only
# match a top-level ui-ideas, which does not exist.
**/ui-ideas/**/*.png
**/ui-ideas/**/*.jpg
**/ui-ideas/**/*.jpeg
visual-WRONGKILL/

# The issue recorder's standalone bundle, copied into each app's public/ by its
# `prebuild` so the live site serves it from its own origin. That origin is the
# point: both sites send a CSP whose script-src is 'self' plus a few Google
# hosts, so the bookmarklet can only load a script the site itself serves.
# BUILD OUTPUT, not source. It is rebuilt from packages/issue-recorder on every
# app build, and a committed copy would go stale against the source beside it.
**/public/__recorder.js
packages/issue-recorder/dist/

# Recorded walks and their drafts (walk exports are tens of MB)
.walks/

# Isolated Gradle homes. Issue #588: three self-hosted runners and every local
# build share this machine, and they corrupt each other inside one ~/.gradle, so
# a build here gets its own with GRADLE_USER_HOME=<worktree>/.gradle-home. About
# a gigabyte of downloaded artifacts, never source.
.gradle-home*/

# Cypress run output: failure screenshots, videos and downloads, written under
# each app's own `cypress/.artifacts/` (the `screenshotsFolder` keys in the two
# cypress.config.ts files put them there rather than in the package root next to
# dist/). Output, not input: CI uploads it as a build artifact and nothing
# reads it back. `**/` for the reason spelled out above this: the pattern has to
# match under both `auntieos-admin/` and `mytribe/web/`, and a slash-bearing
# pattern without it would only match at the repo root, where neither exists.
**/cypress/.artifacts/
